+The file is written next to its final name (`.etl.prom.….tmp`, which the collector ignores),
+made readable by everyone (mode 0644, as the exporter usually runs as another user) and renamed
+into place. A failure to write it is logged (`metrics.not_written`) and never fails the run.
+
 **Reports.** Days are calendar days in `REPORTING_ZONE`, so an order placed at 23:30 UTC in
 summer belongs to the next day in Berlin, and the day of a DST change has 23 or 25 hours.
 
